(78,NULL,'VTS North Sea Canal, The Netherlands','2013-09-01',16950000,0,1,'A Vessel Traffic System for the Port of Amsterdam and the Dutch Ministry of Transport.\nThe port of Amsterdam is connected to the North Sea by means of the North sea Channel. This canal has a length of 31 km. All vessels visiting the port of Amsterdam have to pass through this canal. To safeguard all traffic on the North sea channel the NZK-VTS was build.\nThe canal is used by sea going vessels as well as inland vessels.','VTS','MaritimeControl',NULL,NULL,NULL,157,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,1,0,'2026-09-09 20:42:34.748','2026-09-09 20:42:34.748',2,NULL,1,0),
(79,NULL,'VTS North Sea Canal, The Netherlands - Upgrade contract VTS North Sea Canal for 7 years, The Neth...','2017-12-04',4031000,0,1,'This contract contains a yearly software release as from 2018 to 2022, deliver and maintain for the VTS for the port of Amsterdam that was delivered September 2013.\nA Vessel Traffic System for the Port of Amsterdam.\nThe port of Amsterdam is connected to the North Sea by means of the North sea Channel. This canal has a length of 31 km. All vessels visiting the port of Amsterdam have to pass through this canal. To safeguard all traffic on the North sea channel the NZK-VTS was built.\nThe canal is used by both sea going vessels as well as inland vessels.','VTS','MaritimeControl',NULL,NULL,NULL,157,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,1,0,'2026-09-09 20:42:34.772','2026-09-09 20:42:34.772',2,NULL,1,0),
(80,NULL,'VTS North Sea Canal, The Netherlands - SLC Project IJmuiden, The Netherlands','2015-11-01',5300000,0,1,'The locks in IJmuiden are the entry point into the North Sea Channel for vessels with destination port of Amsterdam. The North Sea Channel links the port of Amsterdam to the North Sea.\nThe ever demanding growth of goods to be transported overseas and the need of lower costs for transport have led to an increase of vessel sizes. Mainly the length but also the width of the vessels have increased over the past decades. The current Noordersluis (North Lock) was constructed in 1929 according to vessel sizes known to men at that time. \nThe current size of the lock constructed in 1929 is too small for the modern sized vessels to guarantee a safe and smooth passage towards the port of Amsterdam. Besides, the current lock is by 2029 at the end of its economic lifetime. \nThe lock extension is of vital importance for the accessibility of the Port of Amsterdam. \nTo maintain Radar and VHF coverage several sensor sites needs to be relocated. To maintain sufficient radar coverage 1 radar is added.','VTS','V3000',NULL,NULL,NULL,157,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,1,0,'2026-09-09 20:42:34.795','2026-09-09 20:42:34.795',2,NULL,1,0),
(81,NULL,'Lease & Upgrade VTS Nijmegen, The Netherlands - Upgrade VTS Nijmegen, The Netherlands','2020-11-01',743300,0,1,'VTS Nijmegen provides radar, AIS, VHF and CCTV coverage at the Waal (river Rhine) east of Nijmegen to the German border. The river Waal is the main inland shipping route between the Port of Rotterdam and Germany. The river Waal belongs to one of the busiest inland waterways in the world.\nBesides the controlling and monitoring of the inland vessel traffic between Germany and the Port of Rotterdam also 2 important intersections are controlled.\n These 2 intersections are the intersection between the river Waal and “het Pannerdens Kanaal” and between the river Waal and the “Maas-Waal kanaal.\nThe control of these 2 intersection is important with respect to safety, security and efficiency because the vessels leaving these “kanaal” cannot see the traffic on the river Waal themselves.','VTS','MaritimeControl',NULL,NULL,NULL,157,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,1,0,'2026-09-09 20:42:34.820','2026-09-09 20:42:34.820',147,NULL,1,0),
(82,NULL,'VTS Amsterdam Rhine Canal','2012-05-01',1548665,0,1,'VTS ARK consists of 1 traffic centre at Wijk bij Duurstede and two lock control stations being Prinses Irenesluizen and the Beatrixsluizen. The Amsterdam Rhine Channel (ARK) has dense vessel traffic. In the Utrecht area two important sectors are monitored, the harbour area Lageweide and the crossing of the channel with the Lek river.','VTS','MaritimeControl',NULL,NULL,NULL,157,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,1,0,'2026-09-09 20:42:34.843','2026-09-09 20:42:34.843',148,NULL,1,0),
