(103,NULL,'Great Barrier Reef VTS system, Australia','2020-01-01',2551000,0,1,'Great Barrier Reef is one of the most beautiful areas from all over the world. Barrier Reef is also a Unesco World heritage site due to its ecological beauty. The barrier reef is also a busy shipping area with a lot of passing vessels. To protect the reef a VTS system is required. This VTS system consist of a total overview of the entire area and includes 5 ports. Tidalis Technologies B.V. delivers and developed the Software, Maritime Control, which is used for the ReefVTS. The ReefVTS system will be provided to Queensland Maritime Services (QMS) by STBV reseller Australian Maritime Services (AMS) Also Tidalis Technologies Ltd. is involved in this project to provide the Port Management function, called Q-ships. ReefVTS consists of: Main Control Centre, Back-up control centre, 5 port VTS’s, AIS network, Q-ship (port Management system), 11 radars, 16 AIS base stations, 10 AIS listeners, 21 working positions, 21 web-viewers, portable replayer, 11 integrated PTZ camera’s, 5 fixed position camera’s and hydro/meteo sensors. Description: ReefVTS requires some specific functions which are directly related to the huge area covered by the ReefVTS-system. 2 of these functions are Ship Encounter','VTS','MaritimeControl',NULL,NULL,NULL,14,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,1,0,'2026-09-09 20:42:35.289','2026-09-09 20:42:35.289',62,NULL,1,0),
